```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Data engineering teams performing per-shard df[col].astype('category') for Parquet compression in time/geo-partitioned or streaming pipelines, coupled with ML teams consuming .cat.codes as integer features across shards without explicit category alignment. Occurs when storage optimization (category dtype for size) silently sets the feature contract that downstream ML consumes.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real bug with severe impact (deltaR2 up to 1.415, R2 collapse to negative) but niche to anti-pattern usage. Not a microbenchmark artifact: L0 shows monotonic dose-response (f=0.0→0.4), exact null boundary (deltaR2=0.000 at f=0), RF cross-check (1.414 vs 1.415), realistic SNR (R2~0.78), and two distinct mechanisms (astype sort vs pyarrow first-seen). However, mature ML teams using sklearn encoders or explicit CategoricalDtype avoid this; the hazard is specific to .cat.codes-as-feature anti-pattern.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Teams must be using .cat.codes directly as features (discouraged practice); Fix is trivial (CategoricalDtype with fixed categories, or proper encoder) but awareness gap exists; Pandas docs document per-file sort behavior but not cross-shard ML hazard; Silent failure mode means teams won't detect without explicit validation; Requires organizational separation between storage (optimizing for size) and ML (consuming codes) to manifest]
RATIONALE: L0 EXP-0080 verifies composition: astype sorts per-shard observed values (100% common codes differ), codes survive Parquet round-trip, pyarrow dict-encode diverges independently. Partial-observation sweep shows deltaR2=0.966 (f=0.1) to 1.415 (f=0.4) with monotonicity; f=0 null boundary exact at 0.000. RF confirms model-agnostic (1.414 vs 1.415). Distinction from Kapoor-Narayanan 2023 leakage is valid: no fitted estimator, contract set by storage cast, not fit-transform. Pandas 3.0.3 docs describe per-file .cat.codes stability but lack cross-shard ML-feature hazard warning (researcher issue-tracker search negative per packet). Actionable guidance: never use .cat.codes across shards without explicit category definition.
```
